{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqepum5450l","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"FeatureBench Docker images are amd64 only so arm64 runs under qemu emulation at about 14 minutes per instance","summary":"FB-1 smoke test verdict (2026-06-15): FeatureBench 0.2.1 (needs Python >=3.12, install via uv) runs locally on Apple Silicon, but its eval Docker images are amd64-only (all 18 fast-split repo images publish a single linux/amd64 manifest, zero arm64). `fb pull`/`fb eval` issue no --platform flag; Docker Desktop auto-emulates via qemu. Gold-patch eval scored green (resolved_rate 1.0, 10/10 FAIL_TO_PASS) confirming the pipeline works — BUT wall-clock is ~13m42s per instance under emulation, single worker. Implication: the 100-instance fast split is ~23h of eval per arm single-threaded locally; multi-instance rollouts want a native x86 box (or heavy local concurrency). FB-2 (fb infer) additionally needs an [llm] block with an API key in config.toml.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T04:31:36.088Z","vec":[0.011894455179572105,0.09483625739812851,-0.009021200239658356,-0.038339097052812576,0.01906673237681389,-0.07700620591640472,-0.10171915590763092,0.006972539704293013,-0.041910238564014435,-0.03206496313214302,-0.023498428985476494,-0.12632298469543457,-0.00207462883554399,0.0018682916415855289,0.07077382504940033,0.034388042986392975,0.07263407856225967,-0.025255111977458,-0.010410908609628677,0.025909490883350372,-0.09226589649915695,-0.013375927694141865,0.004173304419964552,-0.05356225371360779,0.005613242741674185,-0.046048350632190704,-0.11649929732084274,0.028039880096912384,0.03920659050345421,-0.04502994939684868,0.06850741058588028,0.053972769528627396,0.03664926066994667,0.02610817365348339,0.09046909958124161,0.03124377690255642,0.03294111043214798,-0.08314426243305206,-0.10134938359260559,0.0059091029688715935,0.08007848262786865,-0.015197589993476868,-0.037004005163908005,0.014706079848110676,0.05697742477059364,-0.00489692483097